00:41:51,280 --> 00:41:56,830
if your program is basically just like a straight line.

436
00:41:56,830 --> 00:42:06,030
In some sense, if it's very easy to test in a conventional way because there's not a lot of concurrency, there's not a lot of like network chatter, right?

437
00:42:06,030 --> 00:42:11,910
It's just like a small stateless function that does something, and you can write some unit tests for it pretty easily.

438
00:42:11,920 --> 00:42:17,910
That probably doesn't justify the the pain and hassle of trying to test it this way.

439
00:42:17,910 --> 00:42:21,350
If you're running on exotic hardware, like we certainly cannot support you today.

